    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s roster today, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier play with a 75.80 score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against M. P\u00e9rez\u2019s 4.73 xERA and a potent spot in the two-hole. While the raw projections for **Tyler Freeman** (59.24) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.46) trail **Cal Raleigh**, they offer high-floor utility today; **Tyler Freeman** capitalizes on a significant park factor (+14%) and a slow delivery from Peralta that presents a sneaky opportunity for his elite stolen base profile. Conversely, we are navigating a minefield with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, both of whom see their scores severely hampered by elite SP skill ratings (xERA 3.04 and 3.02, respectively), though **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start due to his massive base projection, which buffers against the threat of a tough opponent like Ragans.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Daulton Varsho**, who hovered near the starting threshold but ultimately fell to the bench due to both an unfavorable platoon matchup against McClanahan and an assumed lineup position that limits his run production. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Lawrence Butler**, whose score was buoyed by a 13% platoon edge and favorable wind conditions, despite facing the formidable Wheeler. Owners should remain vigilant regarding **Yainer Diaz**, who remains on the IL, and ensure that secondary assets like **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, and **Drew Gilbert** are being utilized to manage our daily game caps effectively if these starters run into early-inning defensive substitutions.",
